  "body": "### Summary\nAs the MP-list and storage-find parsers' maintainer, I want legacy oracles for `R333a` and `R333b`, so that \"legacy stops at the first storage match, and so does the parser\" is pinned by legacy output, not by reading `MPStorage.m`.\n\n### Scope\n- Run `tooling/legacy-oracle/run-oracle.sh` (Mac) on `R333a` and `R333b` (#766): the MP-list oracle (as `LOT-002/R13u1.oracle.json`, `LOT-002/R95k.oracle.json`) and the storage-find oracle (as `LOT-004/S-find-R13u1.oracle.json`).\n- Add differential tests; `R333b` row 16 (a second storage-subject thread) is the case to pin.\n\n### Sources\n- #333 scope: \"Add a legacy oracle when a parser consumes it\"; Fable review of #766, finding 1.\n- `MPStorage.m:692-736` @ `2440d79`.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- Oracles committed next to their siblings; tests compare the Swift parsers with them; LOT-038 spec cites them.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
